        "lf_sha256": "a9bc657fb926368561ab2657dfbfbf6a7a0ba5b8c2122f8d1fb8510a0a975262"
      },
      "literal_text": "We study the problem of sampling from the probability measure \\mu(\\mathrm{d}x)=Z^{-1}e^{-V(x)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x on \\mathbb{R}^{d}, where V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d}) satisfies, for 0<\\alpha\\leq\\beta, \\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\hskip 20.00003ptx\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\hskip 20.00003pt\\kappa\\coloneqq\\tfrac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,. (1.1) The main result of this paper is the following.",
